 gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:18:21-07:00","id":995270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026#post994973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026 please show them this.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MyACGG/videos/1307544232610550\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/MyACGG/videos/1307544232610550</a></div> </div> </div> </div>...really?<br /> <br /> That doesn't say &quot;Scion&quot; to me in any sense of the word. I'd see more in common with like, Jessica Jones and Luke Cage than I would with this. Even the Dwayne Johnson Hercules film had more Scion going for it.<br /> This is mostly just weird, it doesn't speak to the majesty of the divine or the trials of a person struggling with a powerful destiny that's far beyond their limited ken, fighting to become more than they are and establish a legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T11:22:04-07:00","id":995272,"title":"","content":"Well, it certainly spoke to me! But I'm glad to see that we have such a diversity of takes on the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T13:54:28-07:00","id":995328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995262#post995262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather hand them a copy of American Gods, Anansi Boys, any short story collection containing 'Black Dog' or 'The Monarch of the Glen', or The Ocean at the End of the Lane.<br /> <br /> No offense, but if Anime aesthetic is what you're after, Exalted is totally a game that already exists. You can even run it in a modern setting shard if that strikes your fancy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about the anime aesthetic, it's about the fact that it's a video of an African American gospel choir singing the theme song to a Japanese anime influenced by Judeo-Christian symbology, it shows the syncretic &quot;all myths are true and they're all interacting with each other&quot; nature of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:09:06-07:00","id":995342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995328#post995328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about the anime aesthetic, it's about the fact that it's a video of an African American gospel choir singing the theme song to a Japanese anime influenced by Judeo-Christian symbology, it shows the syncretic &quot;all myths are true and they're all interacting with each other&quot; nature of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already addressed that in the post immediately following it.<br /> <br /> Also, how exactly does showing two different cultures rallying around one anime\u2014which poorly appropriated the imagery of a popular religion whilst communicating none of its context or values\u2014communicate a message of: &quot;All myths are true, and they're interacting with each other.&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:25:32-07:00","id":995347,"title":"","content":"Mostly I'm happy I got to appreciate a piece of weird art and have it remind me of Scion on an emotional and \u00e6sthetic level even if it's not literally about the same things Scion is literally about. I think it might be for the reasons Glamourweaver mentioned. I sang in a gospel choir all through high school despite not being Christian at the time, so I think there's some cognitive dissonance built into the video which evokes those experiences for me. Did any of you guys ever sing gospel, or listen to a lot of gospel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:35:55-07:00","id":995355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995342#post995342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I already addressed that in the post immediately following it.<br /> <br /> Also, how exactly does showing two different cultures rallying around one anime\u2014which poorly appropriated the imagery of a popular religion whilst communicating none of its context or values\u2014communicate a message of: &quot;All myths are true, and they're interacting with each other.&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It shows how people and cultures reapporiate mythological narratives to suit their own needs. In fact Evangelion itself is a prime example of that as its a work of art about Japan's economic and psychological state in the 1990s using the familiar tropes of mecha anime. Sure the Judeo Christian symbology in Eva doesn't mean much besides the connection to matyrdom that is a core theme of the series but the fact that this video has a gospel choir singing the theme shows that things have gone full circle. You go from an anime very loosely using Judeo Christian myth to tell its own story, to Christians turning back around and embracing that new narrative.<br /> <br /> And isn't that what Scion's 2nd edition is about? Loki in 2nd edition is listed as a god of fire due to people confusing him and Loge, it's a translation issue in our world but in the World that translation issue becomes Loki stealing Loge's mantle for himself. Cultures constantly use, recycle, and combine myths to suit their own current needs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995347#post995347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I'm happy I got to appreciate a piece of weird art and have it remind me of Scion on an emotional and \u00e6sthetic level even if it's not literally about the same things Scion is literally about. I think it might be for the reasons Glamourweaver mentioned. I sang in a gospel choir all through high school despite not being Christian at the time, so I think there's some cognitive dissonance built into the video which evokes those experiences for me. Did any of you guys ever sing gospel, or listen to a lot of gospel?</div> </div> </div> </div>It reminds me a lot of Disney's decision to use gospel music for Hercules, their explanation was it that is was a musical about a man trying to become a god, what better musical genre to use then the genre that's entire purpose is to celebrate God?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 10-29-2016, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:40:34-07:00","id":995358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lula</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995347#post995347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly I'm happy I got to appreciate a piece of weird art and have it remind me of Scion on an emotional and \u00e6sthetic level even if it's not literally about the same things Scion is literally about. I think it might be for the reasons Glamourweaver mentioned. I sang in a gospel choir all through high school despite not being Christian at the time, so I think there's some cognitive dissonance built into the video which evokes those experiences for me. Did any of you guys ever sing gospel, or listen to a lot of gospel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I'm wondering if Disney's Hercules including gospel as a device of exposition contributed in some subconscious fashion to your association with this video to Scion.<br /> <br /> Not that it's a bad thing, but I fixate a lot on that sort of thing. Subconscious motives and connections that aren't usually communicated effectively because the person doesn't even notice they're happening.<br /> <br /> I like gospel though, yes. Though I didn't like Evangelion like - at all. It was built up as this big meaningful thing by all of my friends: &quot;Look how deep and symbolic it is! You can tell the creator has a lot to say about life because the Angels turn into a cross when they die!&quot; And just none of that rang true for me, it was an example of someone picking things because they looked good, because those words and visuals are already loaded with emotional content - you don't need to create it yourself, you don't even need to unpack it. That and being a girl I took plenty of umbrage with the show's 'realistic' presentation of female characters, but there's enough points there to write an article.<br /> <br /> So I apologize if I ripped into you too fiercely, you've got positive associations with a thing, and that's great, but I don't think it's really an appropriate 'Scion Aesthetic'. It may be that in your complex thinkspace it drew a whole net of connections that gave you several ideas, but it's not really going to communicate that to someone who doesn't already know what Scion is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:46:48-07:00","id":995359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995355#post995355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shows how people and cultures reapporiate mythological narratives to suit their own needs. In fact Evangelion itself is a prime example of that as its a work of art about Japan's economic and psychological state in the 1990s using the familiar tropes of mecha anime. Sure the Judeo Christian symbology in Eva doesn't mean much besides the connection to matyrdom that is a core theme of the series but the fact that this video has a gospel choir singing the theme shows that things have gone full circle. You go from an anime very loosely using Judeo Christian myth to tell its own story, to Christians turning back around and embracing that new narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or they were paid to. I doubt anyone in that group thinks Eva has any useful commentary to provide on their religion, and if they did they would be offended. It's far more reasonable to expect that the group got paid to sing a song, and the Japanese people present are in awe because - do we really need to get into how Japanese people feel about black people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995355#post995355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And isn't that what Scion's 2nd edition is about? Loki in 2nd edition is listed as a god of fire due to people confusing him and Loge, it's a translation issue in our world but in the World that translation issue becomes Loki stealing Loge's mantle for himself. Cultures constantly use, recycle, and combine myths to suit their own current needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between a translation issue giving Loki a new purview and someone being very depressed, writing something that is depressing, and then slapping the name Loki onto the character because Loki is a name people recognize (name recognition goes a <i>long</i> way in art) and already have complex emotions toward. One of these things attempts to honor the spirit of the narrative, the other one attempts to exploit it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T14:51:34-07:00","id":995360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995355#post995355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It shows how people and cultures reapporiate mythological narratives to suit their own needs. In fact Evangelion itself is a prime example of that as its a work of art about Japan's economic and psychological state in the 1990s using the familiar tropes of mecha anime. Sure the Judeo Christian symbology in Eva doesn't mean much besides the connection to matyrdom that is a core theme of the series but the fact that this video has a gospel choir singing the theme shows that things have gone full circle. You go from an anime very loosely using Judeo Christian myth to tell its own story, to Christians turning back around and embracing that new narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have trouble seeing this as anything other than another weird gimmick, one endemic to Japanese television, surrounding one of the most popular anime they've ever had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:08:42-07:00","id":995371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995359#post995359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or they were paid to. I doubt anyone in that group thinks Eva has any useful commentary to provide on their religion, and if they did they would be offended. It's far more reasonable to expect that the group got paid to sing a song, and the Japanese people present are in awe because - do we really need to get into how Japanese people feel about black people?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a difference between a translation issue giving Loki a new purview and someone being very depressed, writing something that is depressing, and then slapping the name Loki onto the character because Loki is a name people recognize (name recognition goes a <i>long</i> way in art) and already have complex emotions toward. One of these things attempts to honor the spirit of the narrative, the other one attempts to exploit it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to get into to much about Eva, it's my favorite story of all time and I love to talk about it but I want to keep things focused on Scion, but I will say that it is absolutely not meaningful because it has cross lasers and heavy handed Christian symbolism, that is almost entirely window dressing and one of the producers of the series said it was done to make the series visually stand out as Chrisitanity was considered exotic to its targeted Japanese audience. It's meaningful because of what it says about the human heart, the series is entirely about the way people hurt each each other but in the end the pain of being close to someone is worth it as all the joyous moments of life come also from being intimate with others. Director Hideaki Anno was making a statement about the isolated culture of modern Japan and he used the familiar tropes of giant robot anime as a backdrop to tell that story. He did the same thing again in Shin Godzilla, only this time about Japan's state after the Fukishima disaster.<br /> <br /> I also completely disagree with you on the female characters. Eva is a deeply feminist show as pretty much every single scientific and tactical achievement done in that setting was done by a woman. Gendo piggybacks all of Nerv and the Eva project from all the work the women in his life did and he suffers for it in End of Eva.<br /> <br /> But since you say you didn't like Eva at all I'm just going to assume we have completely different tastes amd reasons for being into Scion and that's ok. I am glad that two people with such different opinions can also enjoy Scion, it says a lot about this new edition when it's bringing so many different kinds of people together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 10-29-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T15:46:44-07:00","id":995385,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995371#post995371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to get into to much about Eva, it's my favorite story of all time and I love to talk about it but I want to keep things focused on Scion, but I will say that it is absolutely not meaningful because it has cross lasers and heavy handed Christian symbolism, that is almost entirely window dressing and one of the producers of the series said it was done to make the series visually stand out as Chrisitanity was considered exotic to its targeted Japanese audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you agree then that the mythology doesn't really contribute anything coherent to the series itself, I'm glad we can agree on that much. The issue with this thread and why I responded the way I did is because it was presented as 'This is the aesthetic of Scion', or in other words: &quot;Scion is a setting in which mythological elements are used as window dressing without any real concern for fidelity or the importance the source material has in the hearts and minds of the people who grew up with these cultural legends.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995371#post995371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's meaningful because of what it says about the human heart, the series is entirely about the way people hurt each each other but in the end the pain of being close to someone is worth it as all the joyous moments of life come also from being intimate with others. Director Hideaki Anno was making a statement about the isolated culture of modern Japan and he used the familiar tropes of giant robot anime as a backdrop to tell that story. He did the same thing again in Shin Godzilla, only this time about Japan's state after the Fukishima disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>He also said that Evangelion is meaningless, so you can't say he was 'making a statement'. People interpreted his work in that fashion, and that's fine. The issue is that there are plenty of stories that tell that story, and arguably do it better. Also, the story of humans remaining human and being distinct but close to one another falls a bit flat when you consider that Scion is a game about cultivating a Legend that sets you apart from other humans, with the end result being you either die or you become a god, and thus enter the Overworld and become separated from them forever.<br /> <br /> Can you fit Evangelion's themes into Scion? Yes, but you really need to tailor the story around it, it's in no way inherent to what's going on in Scion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995371#post995371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also completely disagree with you on the female characters. Eva is a deeply feminist show as pretty much every single scientific and tactical achievement done in that setting was done by a woman. Gendo piggybacks all of Nerv and the Eva project from all the work the women in his life did and he suffers for it in End of Eva.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more to feminism than just writing a story where women are successful. Evangelion is sexist not because women don't accomplish anything in the context of the story, it's sexist because the closest thing we get to a realistic female character that we can relate to is Misato, and even she has her moments where she clearly exists for the sake of Hideaki expressing his frustrations with women through the medium of Shinji's relationship with her. All of the women in the show are depicted as, for all of their power, infantile, capricious, and dependent on figures like Gendo or Shinji. Even Asuka has moments of this, and Rei is just... let's not even go there with Rei.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=coNQAucXoNM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=coNQAucXoNM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=coNQAucXoNM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=coNQAucXoNM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This video is not about Evangelion, but it does a very good job of explaining the problem of Power Fantasy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T16:23:50-07:00","id":995418,"title":"","content":"Oh I absolutely can say he was making a statement because he has spoken at great lengths about his goals with Eva and what kind of story it is.<br /> <br /> Anno hasn't ever said Eva was meaningless. I don't know where this idea that he said that keeps coming from but it is a total falsehood. He certainly dislikes the more rabid fan base but he is very proud of the series.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying Evangelion is ripe Scion inspiration. I would say American Gods and WicDiv fits much better, but yes I do think think an American gospel choir singing a Japanese theme to an anime based loosely off Judeo-Christian mythology is a perfect example of the syncreticism of the World's setting. That's all I'm saying.<br /> <br /> I entirely disagree with you on how you see the female characters of Eva, I don't even know where to begin, but I will say that Shinji is not a male power fantasy in any way, shape or form, I don't know how anyone could watch the Tv series and EoE and leave thinking that. He is in fact a deconstruction of the typical anime male hero who falls into the cockpit and magically becomes the world's savior. He fails again and again and his last moment of the series is strangling Asuka while weeping. Not exactly a male power fantasy. None of the women in the series are dependent on Shinji. None of them. Not even Rei. They all have their own rich inner lives and do just fine without him. They accomplish much but are not perfect paragons of virtue by any means, they're human beings with their own faults and insecurities. In fact Shinji places all the responsibility of his well being entirely on other women and this is never portrayed as a good thing. This is spelled out directly to the audience during the Instrumentality sequence in EoE. That's what makes Eva a feminist show, it sees men and women as equally flawed and equally capable of good,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11643,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","user":"Corax","date":". 10-29-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T18:24:56-07:00","id":995463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anno hasn't ever said Eva was meaningless. I don't know where this idea that he said that keeps coming from but it is a total falsehood. He certainly dislikes the more rabid fan base but he is very proud of the series.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SVm65tlhqw8\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SVm65tlhqw8\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SVm65tlhqw8\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SVm65tlhqw8 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This video gets into it, and provides a wealth of sources, all of which I unfortunately don't have the time to dig through right now. He does not say, verbatim, that the show is meaningless, but this is an extrapolation of him saying many other things, among them being the lack of planning that went into any of it - so you can claim death of the author, but you can't say they were statements he intended to make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm not saying Evangelion is ripe Scion inspiration. I would say American Gods and WicDiv fits much better, but yes I do think think an American gospel choir singing a Japanese theme to an anime based loosely off Judeo-Christian mythology is a perfect example of the syncreticism of the World's setting. That's all I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>So by that reasoning I could create a thread with this same title linking to the Italian intro theme to My Little Pony, after all, it appropriates Greco-Roman mythical creatures and includes an Italian singer singing the theme song in her native language, we've gone full circle and it's a perfect example of the interaction between pantheons in the setting.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's really true though, in fact I think you could pretty much do that with just about everything, especially in America which is a melting pot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I will say that Shinji is not a male power fantasy in any way, shape or form, I don't know how anyone could watch the Tv series and EoE and leave thinking that.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is a power fantasy because he is literally the most important character in the entire series. Absolutely everything in it revolves around him, his actions, and his inaction. He also happens to be the audience and in many ways, in my opinion, a mirror of the author and the issues he was facing at that point in his life (Anno had/has serious problems with depression, anxiety, isolation, etc). When you take a character and make 'him' the audience, even if you're making fun of that audience and yourself, and then give them infinite power and responsibility, that is a <b>power</b> <i>fantasy</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is in fact a deconstruction of the typical anime male hero who falls into the cockpit and magically becomes the world's savior. He fails again and again and his last moment of the series is strangling Asuka while weeping. Not exactly a male power fantasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but he still falls into the cockpit and magically becomes the world's savior. Also the last bit? Doesn't exactly help your stance on the series not being sexist when Asuka literally just stands there while Shinji strangles her in a fit of sexual frustration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the women in the series are dependent on Shinji. None of them. Not even Rei.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Everyone</i> in the series is dependent on Shinji, the girls are effectively his subordinates in that they're not going to be the ones who stop the Angels because they're not the chosen one. On more than one occasion they have to be rescued by him, are reminded of how inferior they are compared to him, and just about every one of them has their problems sexualized. You'll honestly be hard pressed to find an anime that <i>isn't</i> sexist from that decade, and there's a reason why you'll see the girls from Evangelion front in center in: &quot;Me! Me! Me!&quot;, because of how sexualized they are in that show. The women in Evangelion are, to me, as a woman, unrelateable. Often their damage boils down to wanting to be intimate with Gendo - or whatever weird relationship is going on with Shinji and his surrogate mom. Rei is effectively a distant and detached doll while members of the cast and the audience sexualize her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They all have their own rich inner lives and do just fine without him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only one who I can think of that has a life that doesn't revolve around Shinji is Akagi, and it revolves around his father, instead. You could make a case for Rei, but her life also revolves around Gendo. It's dehumanizing and disturbing in a way that the male cast never experiences, and the entire time I spent watching it with my friend I was given less the impression that this was a real person with real issues to be sorted out, and more that damaged women were being sexualized for the sake of the audience. It was like reading a Piers Anthony book as a kid, and then revisiting his books ten years later once you actually understand what's going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/994973-the-next-time-someone-asks-you-what-scion-2e-s-\u00e6sthetic-is-\u2026?p=995418#post995418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They accomplish much but are not perfect paragons of virtue by any means, they're human beings with their own faults and insecurities. In fact Shinji places all the responsibility of his well being entirely on other women and this is never portrayed as a good thing. This is spelled out directly to the audience during the Instrumentality sequence in EoE. That's what makes Eva a feminist show, it sees men and women as equally flawed and equally capable of good,</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need them to be perfect paragons of virtue, I need them to be relatable, to have ambitions other than having sex with their boss/child ward, and to not be dolls for the audience to lust after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","user":"Solana","date":". 10-29-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T19:13:04-07:00","id":995474,"title":"","content":"I feel really guilty for turning this thread into a roast of Evangelion, and don't think that's very fair to Lula. If anyone wants to poke me about it in PMs that's cool, or even publicly on my profile, but for now I think we should turn this into a thread of Scion Aesthetics using the rational of the OP video, and try to instead have fun with it instead of being critical of it.<br /> <br /> So, I present my vote for best Scion Aesthetic: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y8pYfCtNPzA\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y8pYfCtNPzA</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:19:50-07:00","id":995823,"title":"","content":"I don't really care for Evangelion but I enjoy the result of this kind of thing. I think one can be a bit overly reliant on textual analysis with regards to intentions for a lot of things and easily ignore how important the reception of a thing is.<br /> <br /> If the Christian symbolism of Eva is not of deep textual interest to Hideaki Ano, that's interesting. What about when it is significant and relevant to Christians watching it? Their takeaway is certainly different than Anno's, and I'd argue it's more interesting, because it's fascinating to consider all the subtle and indirect ways these things can be meaningful to us.<br /> <br /> That works in two ways with this video. I can't speak to that choir's experience of Evangelion, but even if it's as simple and straightforward as &quot;we really enjoyed the opening song&quot; I think that's interesting and meaningful, too.<br /> <br /> It also can be significant in how we receive it, and what it means to us. I think Lula provided a great example in his personal reception of this, as the question of &quot;why is this meaningful to you?&quot; Is actually a very complex question with a lot of interesting answers, including personal experience with gospel, Evangelion itself, religious affinity and the divide between secular personal ideology and the reception of gospel in that secular perspective, race, cross-cultural experience and other things. There's a lot of interesting stuff to unpack and explore in the reception of the thing, even if you think the thing itself is fairly simple.<br /> <br /> And I think this taps into a really interesting space that Scion exists in too. These gods and mythologies, almost all of them do not have a &quot;canon&quot; of some kind. They have tendencies, and our notions of canon are largely limitations of the texts we derive them from.<br /> <br /> Like, think about how Scion is a syncretic work itself and how syncretism as a practice is not an austere, refined objective and distant process, but a messy, intimate and personal process that has a lot to do with how we receive and value things. <br /> <br /> So for me, as a Harlem kid who grew up with lots of kids that watched anime and constructed facets of their identity from it, Evangelion and this video have a personal value and express a complex relationship between people and stories that speaks to Scion in my eye.<br /> <br /> The gods are themselves composed of stories, because those are how we derive identity and value from them, and on a personal level, know them through these stories. <br /> <br /> The personal conflicts characters will have with the gods IMO mirrors the complex relationship between people, faith and stories and that seems like one of the things that will make the game really awesome.<br /> <br /> so I like it for that reason. I like the actual singing and the idea of it, and what it can represent to people. To me, that goes beyond a simplistic idea of multiculturalism that is just A + B and speaks more to how we can have complex relationships with things culturally and personally, regardless of what the author may have wanted or failed to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}